From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Biggart <swbiggart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:43:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/46] flashnext cuda: an aborted communicator releases the
 round graph first

A graph that captured NCCL collectives holds persistent plans, and
ncclCommAbort waits without a bound until every such graph is destroyed
(commDestroySync polls localPersistentRefs). With the round graph held
by the engine, a peer lost during a replay, a capture or between rounds
would hang the surviving rank in the abort instead of returning
RankDisconnected or RankTimeout. The cache that captures a
communicator's collectives now registers a release that the abort runs
first: it ends an open capture, frees its graph and destroys the
executable, so NCCL's abort can drain and return.
